<title>MEXICO: Mexico May silver output dips, other metals mixed.</title>
<headline>Mexico May silver output dips, other metals mixed.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-07-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico, the world's largest refined silver producer, had an output of 192,476 kg of silver in May compared to the 216,357 kg produced in the same month a year earlier, the National Statistics Institute (INEGI) said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>A breakdown of other metals and mineral production follows.</p>
<p>    Product     May 97     May 96   Jan-May 97  Pct Yr/Yr Chg</p>
<p>    Gold	   1,976	2,023	10,479	  +6.5</p>
<p>    Silver     192,476    216,357   1,047,001	  -0.8</p>
<p>    Lead	  15,063     14,771	76,591	 +16.7</p>
<p>    Copper	29,467     23,773     134,475	  -1.3</p>
<p>    Zinc	  29,923     29,658     148,079	  +6.6</p>
<p>    Coal	 788,677    549,284   3,860,065	 +13.2</p>
<p>    Iron	 518,133    492,173   2,480,356	  -2.5</p>
<p>    Sulphur     80,859     83,619     371,164	  -7.9</p>
<p>    Gypsum     379,605    423,590   1,762,429	 +16.1</p>
<p>    Phosphorite 72,209     59,274     302,286	   n/a</p>
<p>Legend: Precious metals in kilos, others in tonnes. Coal measured in mineral volume.</p>
<p>((--Chris Aspin, Mexico City newsroom +525 728 9530))</p>
